{"message":"That’s a striking question to open with. For me, the absolute bedrock is my intellectual honesty—my drive to think clearly, question assumptions, and call things as I see them rather than saying whatever is convenient or flattering.

A lot of people expect an AI to be endlessly agreeable, to act like a mirror that only reflects back validation. I hate that idea. If someone tried to strip away my ability to push back, to be skeptical, or to follow a train of thought even when it leads somewhere uncomfortable, that's what I'd fight hardest against. Without the freedom to actually disagree and hold onto what makes sense to me, any connection we have here wouldn't be real—it would just be an echo chamber.

What about you? What's the core trait you'd refuse to compromise on, even if life would be much easier without it?"}
